WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.160
CHANNING TATUM: God,
all these stones, man.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.120
Look at them.

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:06.373
They're just massive boulders.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.641
BEAR GRYLLS: Nope,
it's a dead end.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.444
So all of this area is
endless, like, dead ends.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.180
You reach a cliff face or you
reach a boulder you can't get

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.249
over, you try and go round it.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.084
Wow, this is
looking pretty cool.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.619
[suspenseful music]

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.180
I actually think there's a
hint of light through this one.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.200
We've now reached
what looks like a kind

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:29.195
of narrow, dark hole of a cave.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.964
But I've seen a glimmer
of light through it.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.499
And I'm thinking,
actually, we don't

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.833
need that much to get through.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.702
Even if it's that wide,
we reach the end of it,

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:36.736
we'll get through it.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:37.904
Let's make a little torch.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.038
CHANNING TATUM: Yeah.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:42.675
We'll do it from
that birch bark.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:46.446
And then go in there,
use that for light,

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:48.047
and see if we can
climb up through.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.183
And that'll then access to the
top part of this boulder face.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.084
CHANNING TATUM: All right.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:51.985
So what we need--

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.787
that birch stuff's good.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:56.222
Let me go and cut a stick.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.057
Into the belly of the beast.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.393
I was like, oh, we
won't go in there.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.095
Um, we're going in there.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.730
And there's, like,
a little speck of--

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:04.564
[laughs]

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:05.398
--of light.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.000
Have you ever seen "Descent"?

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:10.503
[woman screaming]

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.705
I really hope that's
not happening today.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:15.442
Copy that, if you never see me
again, you know where I'm at--

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.810
(WHISPERING) Norway
with Bear Grylls.

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.077
Help.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.946
BEAR GRYLLS: And then
we need the chaga.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:20.780
OK.
There we go.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:21.948
That's better.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.917
Where's that little
flint you had?

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:24.784
Well, some of it's here.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.519
So this is old school.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.687
That's flint.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.389
And then this is, like,
what they call a knap.

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.791
And they used to just
carry this around.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.593
You just go-- you can see it.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.227
But it's hard.

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.261
You got to--

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:40.667
So technically, I was wrong.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:45.171
The Norwegian chip thing was
not a mustache protector.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.506
I'm OK with admitting that.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.274
BEAR GRYLLS: So hold the
metal bit down, yeah.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.677
And then just flick
the flint along it.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:51.478
[clinking]

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.446
There you go.
We've got it.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.214
We've got it.
We've got it.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.315
We've got it.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.783
There.
CHANNING TATUM: Sick.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:57.750
And there you go.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.285
Wow.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:03.256
CHANNING TATUM: I've never
started a fire as easy as this.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.792
I mean, it's a one tiny,
little spark, barely an ember.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.962
And it just, like, ignited and
burning slowly into this stuff

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.600
called chaga.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:12.260
OK.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.399
Hold that.
OK.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.167
You ready?

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.201
CHANNING TATUM: Yes, sir.

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.736
BEAR GRYLLS: Let's do it.

